+Normalize surrounding whitespace and uppercase ASCII letters before lookup. Serial-number punctuation remains significant. Return the snapshot date even when no matching record exists. Lookups execute against the embedded SQLite index; the query path is `SELECT ... WHERE serial = ?` after normalization, with an index on the normalized serial column.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Lookup backend | Local embedded SQLite index | On-site HTTPS directory; managed search service | Predictable lookups with no service to run. Each kiosk validates and rebuilds its own index on snapshot arrival, keeping all index maintenance inside the registry component. Meets HLD tenet of no runtime network access. |
+| Snapshot activation | Atomic swap after full validation | Incremental update; lazy rebuild | Failed import must leave last valid snapshot available. Atomic swap ensures no partially imported records are exposed. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. ✅ Lookup backend selected as local embedded SQLite index
+
+### Deferred
+1. Index rebuild performance budget and progress reporting for 150 MB snapshots
